## 10. Suggested Build Order

1. Prompt 0 (scaffold) → 1 (shell) → 2–4 (home hero/occasion/trend) — get a demo-able landing page fast, using mock JSON only for these purely visual sections.
2. **Prompt 11 (backend) before 5/5a/5b** — since New Arrivals, Listing, and PDP are dynamic-only, stand up the Products API and seed the DB first, so the frontend never touches static product data.
3. Prompt 5 (dynamic New Arrivals/Featured grids) → 5a (dynamic Listing) → 5b (dynamic PDP), all wired to the live API from the start.
4. Prompt 9 (auth) in parallel, since Cart/Wishlist depend on session state.
5. Prompt 7 (cart) → 8 (wishlist) — wire to Zustand + localStorage first, swap to API-backed persistence once auth exists.
6. Prompt 6 (brand story/testimonials/CTA) and Prompt 10 (About/Contact) — low-risk, can slot in anytime.
7. Prompt 12–13 (OTP auth backend + payments).
8. Prompt 14 (QA) — final pass before launch.
